\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Z-residual diagnostic $p$-values for the response-family sensitivity analysis using the same HNB-generated representative dataset as in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {M-sec:sim-nl} of the main text. The HNB-log and HNB-linear rows correspond to the models considered in the main text, while the NB-log and NB-linear rows are added here to assess the effect of response-family misspecification. Because the response is discrete and RSP Z-residuals depend on auxiliary randomization, we report median upper-bound $p$-values\nobreakspace  {}(Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {M-eqn:uppvalue-median}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}) for the posterior and ISCV RSP Z-residual tests. The AOV and Bartlett (BL) tests are applied against $X_1$. The logarithmic form is marked ``Wrong'' for the NB family because the $X_1$-dependent hurdle probability is improperly absorbed into the NB mean structure (see text).}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sens_family_function}{{1}{4}{Z-residual diagnostic $p$-values for the response-family sensitivity analysis using the same HNB-generated representative dataset as in Section~\ref {M-sec:sim-nl} of the main text. The HNB-log and HNB-linear rows correspond to the models considered in the main text, while the NB-log and NB-linear rows are added here to assess the effect of response-family misspecification. Because the response is discrete and RSP Z-residuals depend on auxiliary randomization, we report median upper-bound $p$-values~(Eq.~\eqref {M-eqn:uppvalue-median}) for the posterior and ISCV RSP Z-residual tests. The AOV and Bartlett (BL) tests are applied against $X_1$. The logarithmic form is marked ``Wrong'' for the NB family because the $X_1$-dependent hurdle probability is improperly absorbed into the NB mean structure (see text)}{table.1}{}}
